# Broker / trading API keys
# See CLAUDE.md's "Broker Layer" section and FINAL_ANALYSIS.md Section 6/6a for what's real vs
# stub. Only Alpaca reads its credentials from these env vars directly - every other broker's
# credentials are entered through the Setup Wizard / Settings UI and stored encrypted in the DB
# (brokerConnections table); the env vars below for those brokers exist only where the app's own
# code or its secrets registry (server.ts's SECRET_SPECS) already references them.

# Alpaca - REAL, the only broker that can trade fully unattended (paper or live).
ALPACA_API_KEY=
ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=
# Historical-bar cache tail freshness (2026-10-09). Tuning knob, NOT an env var: lives in
# config/tradingSafety.json as "quantBarsTailFreshnessToleranceMs" (default 259200000 = 72h).
# HistoricalDataGateway.ensureBars() accepts a count/coverage-sufficient cache for a
# present-time request only when the newest cached bar is within this tolerance of now;
# a stale tail (e.g. a 7-day-old newest bar from an old-but-large cache) falls through to a
# provider refresh instead. Historical end-date requests (backtest/replay windows ending
# more than this tolerance before now) are exempt. Provider failure or an empty provider
# response surfaces honestly (DATA_STALE/PROVIDER_ERROR) - stale data is never relabeled fresh.
# ensureBars() in-flight coalescing liveness (2026-10-10). Tuning knob, NOT an env var: lives
# in config/tradingSafety.json as "quantBarsCoalesceEntryMaxAgeMs" (default 300000 = 5 min).
# Concurrent ensureBars() calls for the same symbol/timeframe/window share one in-flight
# provider fetch. The inner provider call has no timeout/cancel path, so a stalled fetch
# would otherwise wedge the window's coalescing entry forever; past this age the entry is
# evicted with a loud warn and a later caller starts a fresh fetch.
# Optional. Default is the live IEX top-of-book stream. Paper API keys typically use this same
# URL. Sandbox-only keys: wss://stream.data.sandbox.alpaca.markets/v2/iex
ALPACA_DATA_STREAM_URL=
# When true, BrokerManager.setLiveMode(live=true) refuses (in addition to LIVE phrase + LIVE_ARM).
# Does not by itself force Alpaca paper URLs — keep paperMode aligned in Settings.
# Boot / UI preselect for Market Execution (SIMULATOR | PAPER | LIVE). PAPER_TRADING_ONLY=true
# demotes LIVE → PAPER. This is the single env source Mission Control reads on startup.
ARGUS_TRADING_MODE=PAPER
PAPER_TRADING_ONLY=true
# Declared capital intent for the pre-market readiness gate (2026-10-05). The readiness gate's
# capital-profile node asserts settings.budget (the budget RiskEngine gate 23 actually enforces)
# equals this value; a mismatch fails tradingReady with BUDGET_MISMATCH instead of trading on the
# wrong number (the $2K-intended vs $100K-runtime incident class). Unset = intent unverified
# (node reports notApplicable, still passing). This never changes sizing itself.
# ARGUS_EXPECTED_BUDGET=2000
# When true, skip Vite/static Web UI; trading core + REST API still run (npm run dev:headless).
# ARGUS_HEADLESS=true

# Active broker on boot. BrokerManager.initialize() reads this the same way regardless of entry
# point (npm run dev, dev:server-only, start:engine, or the argus-cli spawn path — one process
# boots the engine either way). Accepts a broker id (internal_paper | alpaca | ibkr_gateway |
# ibkr_web | ibkr | coinbase) or display name (e.g. "IBKR Gateway (Socket)").
#
# Precedence on every boot:
#   1. ARGUS_FORCE_ENV_BROKER_ON_BOOT=true -> always this broker, ignoring any UI selection.
#   2. Otherwise, the last broker selected via Settings > Brokers > SET ACTIVE (persisted to
#      settings.selectedBroker) wins, so a runtime UI switch survives a restart as before.
#   3. Otherwise (fresh DB, nothing ever selected via the UI) -> this broker is the default.
ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER=ibkr_gateway
# See precedence above. false (default) lets a UI broker switch persist across restarts;
# true always re-activates ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER on boot regardless of what was last selected.
ARGUS_FORCE_ENV_BROKER_ON_BOOT=false
# Crypto Expansion Phase 13 (2026-09-22). SEPARATE from ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER above - crypto orders
# (a registered symbol in config/cryptoInstruments.json, e.g. BTC-USD/ETH-USD) route to THIS
# broker if set; every other order (equities) is completely unaffected and keeps using
# ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER as before. "If not provided, uses common broker" (explicit design intent):
# leaving this unset means a crypto order falls back to the common active broker above, which does
# not support crypto execution - RiskEngine gate 12 (market_hours) then correctly reports
# PAPER_BROKER_UNAVAILABLE and blocks it. This is the safe, fail-closed default.
# Accepted values: only 'crypto_paper' is currently a real, usable target (CryptoPaperBroker.ts -
# PAPER/RESEARCH only, fractional BTC-USD/ETH-USD, no live venue). 'coinbase' is explicitly
# REFUSED even though CoinbaseBroker reports crypto:true - it is LIVE-only by design (placeOrder()
# refuses in paper, no sandbox) and must never become a PAPER crypto execution path. Any other/
# unregistered value is ignored (falls back to the common broker, same as unset).
ARGUS_CRYPTO_ACTIVE_BROKER=

# Configurable Execution Broker Support (2026-09-29). Per-broker execution capability flags -
# separate from ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER's SELECTION above. Selecting a broker (ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER /
# Settings > Brokers) says WHICH adapter to use; these flags say WHETHER this deployment/operator
# is actually allowed to execute through it. This is deliberately never inferred from geography -
# Argus does not own regulatory/eligibility decisions (e.g. a Canada-resident operator with a
# non-eligible Alpaca account, or a US-resident operator who simply prefers IBKR) - the operator
# sets these explicitly. A flag being true does NOT mean live trading is enabled or that Argus has
# verified account eligibility; PAPER_TRADING_ONLY/LIVE_NO_GO remain the separate, authoritative
# live-trading gates and are completely unaffected by these flags.
#
# Defaults intentionally differ: ALPACA_EXECUTION_ENABLED defaults false (an operator must
# explicitly opt in to Alpaca execution - e.g. after confirming real US brokerage eligibility).
# IBKR_EXECUTION_ENABLED defaults true, preserving this deployment's existing IBKR-first default
# behavior unchanged for every current .env that doesn't set it.
#
# If ARGUS_ACTIVE_BROKER (or a runtime POST /api/v1/brokers/active call) selects a broker whose
# execution flag is false, BrokerManager refuses to activate it - fail-closed with a clear
# ALPACA_EXECUTION_DISABLED / IBKR_EXECUTION_DISABLED reason, never a silent fallback to a
# different broker (a silent fallback could reroute real order intent to an unintended adapter).
ALPACA_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false
IBKR_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true

# Market data provider, independent of the execution broker above. Historically Argus derived the
# live quote/tick backend entirely from whichever broker was ACTIVE for order execution (IBKR
# active -> IBKR quotes; anything else -> Alpaca quotes) - this coupled two genuinely separate
# concerns. Setting MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER explicitly overrides that derivation, so a deployment can
# run e.g. Alpaca market data with IBKR execution, or vice versa, without touching strategies,
# RiskEngine, or OMS. Leave unset to preserve the exact prior behavior (data backend derived from
# the active execution broker) - this is a purely additive override, not a required setting.
# Accepted values: alpaca | ibkr_gateway. Blank/unset = derive from the active execution broker
# (unchanged default). An unrecognized value is ignored with a warning, same fail-closed-to-default
# posture as ARGUS_CRYPTO_ACTIVE_BROKER above.
MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=

# IBKR delayed-data research feed (2026-09-29). Off by default - zero behavior change. Real
# background: an isolated diagnostic (scripts/ibkr_market_data_diagnostic.ts) found this account's
# fee-waived real-time entitlement does not currently reach the IB Gateway API (code 10089 on
# AAPL/MSFT/NVDA/SPY/QQQ), while IBKR's own delayed-data fallback (reqMarketDataType(3)) works
# cleanly - real BID/ASK/LAST at ~1s latency, informational code 10167, no entitlement error. When
# IBKR_DELAYED_DATA_RESEARCH_ENABLED=true, IbkrSocketSession calls reqMarketDataType(3) once per
# session so delayed ticks actually populate MarketDataWorker's ISOLATED delayed-quote store
# (getDelayedQuote() - diagnostics/research/dashboards/PAPER-analysis only). Per IBKR's own API
# guide this does not force a genuinely live-entitled symbol down to delayed (live entitlement, if
# any, still reports marketDataType=1/REALTIME) - watch the real callback rather than assume, since
# none of this deployment's tested symbols currently carry live entitlement to verify that half.
IBKR_DELAYED_DATA_RESEARCH_ENABLED=false

# Reserved, NOT implemented. There is no code path anywhere in this codebase that lets delayed
# data satisfy RiskEngine gate 13 (data_freshness) or reach any live/paper trade decision,
# regardless of this flag's value - that isolation is structural (delayed ticks live only in
# MarketDataWorker's separate delayedQuotes map; getLatestPrice()/getLatestPriceAgeMs(), the only
# two things gate 13 reads, never consult it - see MarketDataWorker.test.ts's own regression test)
# and does not depend on this flag. It exists only to document the policy explicitly: letting
# delayed data feed a real trade decision is a genuine architecture change requiring explicit
# review against ARGUS_ARCHITECTURE_PROTECTION.md's protected RiskEngine gate list, never a flag flip.
IBKR_DELAYED_DATA_TRADING_ENABLED=false

# Interactive Brokers — default transport is IB Gateway Desktop / TWS TCP socket
# (paper 4002 / 7497). See config/ibkrConnection.json. No browser login required for socket mode.
# Optional override: IBKR_CONNECTION_MODE=socket|web_api
# IBKR_CONNECTION_MODE=socket
# Legacy Client Portal Web API (HTTPS :5000) only when mode=web_api:
IBKR_GATEWAY_URL=https://localhost:5000/v1/api
# Optional Client Portal install path (web_api only). npm run dev does NOT open a browser unless
# IBKR_OPEN_BROWSER=true.
IBKR_GATEWAY_PATH=
# IBKR_OPEN_BROWSER=false

# Questrade - NOT FUNCTIONAL. Questrade's official API restricts order-placement access to
# Questrade-approved partner developers; a third-party retail app (this one) can only ever get
# account/market-data access, never real order execution - QuestradeBroker.placeOrder() throws by
# design, and BrokerManager refuses to let it become the active (order-placing) broker regardless
# of what's configured here. These two vars are declared in server.ts's secrets registry for a
# possible future read-only integration, but nothing in the codebase reads them yet.
QUESTRADE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
QUESTRADE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Coinbase Advanced Trade - NOT FUNCTIONAL. CoinbaseBroker.ts is a genuine placeholder
# (authenticate() always returns true, placeOrder() throws 'Not implemented') - unlike Questrade,
# there's no regulatory blocker here, it's simply unbuilt. These vars match Coinbase's real
# Advanced Trade API key shape but nothing in the codebase reads them yet either.
COINBASE_API_KEY=
COINBASE_API_SECRET=

# News & market data providers
# 2026-09-10: FundamentalAgent/MacroAgent are primarily AlphaVantage-sourced (free tier: 25
# req/day, shared - see AlphaVantageBudget.ts) - that cap was confirmed live to exhaust every
# session, silencing both agents' votes. FMP_API_KEY (FundamentalAgent, free tier: 250 req/day -
# FmpBudget.ts) and FRED_API_KEY (MacroAgent, free/no-payment authoritative U.S. government source
# - no budget tracker needed at this call volume) are now real, wired fallbacks, only ever
# attempted after AlphaVantage has already given up for the day. Neither requires a paid plan.
ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=
POLYGON_API_KEY=
FINNHUB_API_KEY=
FMP_API_KEY=
FRED_API_KEY=

# AI provider API keys
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
KIMI_API_KEY=
GROK_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# JEV_API_KEY: TypeSafe AI's Jev decision model (research spike, 2026-10-05) — a "System One"
# model that returns typed probabilistic answers (yes/no, choice, score) instead of generating
# text. $0.042/1M input tokens, output free. Intended for cheap classification/triage in the
# confidence-gated routing layer, NOT as a chat LLM replacement. TYPESAFE_API_KEY also works
# (the vendor's own env name). Optional: JEV_BASE_URL to override https://api.typesafe.ai.
JEV_API_KEY=

# Authentication and secrets
# Do NOT deploy with the values below - they are placeholders, not real credentials.
# Generate real values with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
AUTH_USERNAME=admin
AUTH_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_generate_a_real_password
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_crypto_randomBytes
AUTH_SESSION_TTL_DAYS=3650
ENCRYPTION_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_generate_with_crypto_randomBytes

# CLI session login (when AUTH_PASSWORD is set on the engine):
# Prefer ARGUS_CLI_USER / ARGUS_CLI_PASSWORD, or reuse AUTH_USERNAME / AUTH_PASSWORD above.
# Then: ./argus login  →  saves data/.argus_cli_session (never commit that file).
# ARGUS_DEV_TOKEN is ignored by the server when AUTH_PASSWORD is set — do not use it as a bypass.
# ARGUS_CLI_USER=
# ARGUS_CLI_PASSWORD=
# ARGUS_CLI_SESSION_FILE=   # optional override; default data/.argus_cli_session

# Remote mobile (Tailscale / LAN): with AUTH_PASSWORD set, the server listens on 0.0.0.0 by default.
# Without auth, the server binds to 127.0.0.1 only. Override for dev-only remote access:
# ARGUS_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Optional operator alerting (Discord webhook URL or Telegram bot sendMessage URL).
# AlertingService posts JSON { content: "..." } on kill-switch, ORDER_EXECUTED, and process boot.
# Also dispatches to CRUD-managed webhooks via /api/v1/webhooks when configured.
ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional runtime configuration
ACTIVE_LLM=gemini
NODE_ENV=development
DISABLE_HMR=false

# Optional: OpenAlice external verification (read-only, non-blocking second opinion - see
# OPENALICE_INTEGRATION_AUDIT.md). `npm run dev` starts OpenAlice Guardian from the sibling
# checkout (OPENALICE_PATH / OPENALICE_REPO_PATH, default ..\OpenAlice) and waits until
# http://127.0.0.1:47332/mcp accepts MCP before Node boots. That URL must expose issue_create
# and inbox_read — a trading MCP is the wrong server. Skip spawn with ARGUS_SKIP_OPENALICE=true
# or ENABLE_OPENALICE=false. OpenAlice never
# receives broker credentials and cannot place Argus trades.
OPENALICE_ENABLED=true
OPENALICE_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:47332/mcp
OPENALICE_REPO_PATH=
# Keep a custom OPENALICE_MCP_URL instead of Guardian (Argus will FAIL if tools are wrong).
# ARGUS_KEEP_OPENALICE_MCP_URL=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ECOSYSTEM PATHS (absolute paths to sibling research repos — NOT vendored into Argus)
# Used only by `npm run dev` → scripts/ecosystem-dev.ts. Missing dirs warn and continue.
# `npm run dev:core` skips vibe/autohedge/Fincept and uses the prior Chronos/Ollama/OpenAlice/IBKR launcher.
#
# TRUST: Argus is sole execution authority. vibe-trading / autohedge / OpenAlice / FinceptTerminal
# are untrusted read-only research/verification. They never receive Argus broker credentials for
# order placement and never bypass RiskEngine / OMS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VIBE_TRADING_PATH=C:\WorkProjects\vibe-trading
AUTOHEDGE_PATH=C:\WorkProjects\autohedge
OPENALICE_PATH=C:\WorkProjects\OpenAlice
FINCEPT_TERMINAL_PATH=C:\WorkProjects\FinceptTerminal

# ECOSYSTEM TOGGLES (orchestrator only — does not change RiskEngine / live path)
ENABLE_VIBE_TRADING_MCP=true
ENABLE_AUTOHEDGE_WORKER=true
ENABLE_OPENALICE=true
# Fincept: require explicit FINCEPT_CMD (no invented default CLI). Leave false until configured.
ENABLE_FINCEPT_TERMINAL=false
# FINCEPT_CMD=path-or-args for the Fincept process (whitespace-separated)

# Fincept advisory read (2026-09-07, distinct from ENABLE_FINCEPT_TERMINAL above): read-only,
# text-only VIX/index context read from an already-running Fincept Terminal's cache.db into
# MacroAgent's reasoning. Does not launch Fincept, never touches confidence/side/RiskEngine/OMS.
# Fails silently (no context attached) when Fincept isn't running - see FinceptCacheAdapter.ts.
ENABLE_FINCEPT_CACHE_ADVISORY=false
# FINCEPT_CACHE_DB_PATH=override for the auto-detected cache.db path (Windows default:
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\com.fincept.terminal\data\cache.db)

# Optional overrides:
# VIBE_TRADING_MCP_PORT=8900
# VIBE_TRADING_MCP_ARGS=--transport http --port 8900
# AUTOHEDGE_CMD=
# AUTOHEDGE_WORKSPACE_DIR=
#
# AutoHedge safety: ecosystem-dev ALWAYS forces WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY="" and SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# in the child process so this launcher cannot enable on-chain execution. Do not put funded
# wallet keys in Argus .env expecting AutoHedge to trade under npm run dev.

# Optional: additive quant decision layer (src/server/quant/, QuantSignalAgent.ts). Off by
# default - zero behavior change for anyone who doesn't set this. When true, real regime/market-
# context assessments run on a timer for actively-tracked symbols and QuantSignalAgent
# participates in Chief Trader consensus as agent:'QuantEngine' (a weight for that exact name
# already exists in ChiefTraderAgent.ts, unused until this is enabled).
QUANT_ENGINE_ENABLED=false
# Optional: NEWS_AGENT_MODE overrides config/deskIntelligence.json newsAgentMode.
# CATALYST_ONLY (default) = FinBERT + catalysts, no News TRADE_IDEA votes.
# ACTIVE_VOTE = NewsAgent may vote into ChiefTrader (still 0.75 / min-2 + RiskEngine).
# NEWS_AGENT_MODE=ACTIVE_VOTE   # default in deskIntelligence.json; set CATALYST_ONLY to silence ideas
# Optional research Python (VectorBT). Research-only — never places orders. Leave unset to use
# the system python. ARGUS_PYTHON=python
# pip install -r requirements-research.txt
# pip install -U "vectorbt[rust]"  # optional acceleration; app stays usable without Rust.
# Milliseconds between evaluation cycles. Optional - defaults to 300000 (5 min) if unset.
QUANT_ENGINE_INTERVAL_MS=
# 2026-10-09 (P2 scheduler): bounded priority quant scheduler (src/server/scheduling/
# quantPriorityScheduler.ts). Off by default - when true, QuantSignalAgent.runCycle admits its
# universe to priority queues (P0 urgent mover / P1 promoted / P2 normal / P3 background) with
# per-priority assessment deadlines and separate bounded pools for quant workers vs data
# fetches, instead of the legacy snapshot+worker-pool fan-out. Control-plane only: never
# changes strategy selection, thresholds, consensus, RiskEngine, OMS, or broker behavior.
# Knobs live in config/tradingSafety.json (quantScheduler*), not here.
QUANT_PRIORITY_SCHEDULER_ENABLED=false
# Off by default. A strategy-sourced idea normally requires >=1 real closed live trade for that
# exact strategy before it's allowed to emit (real EV/win-rate check, ARGUS_PHASE16_READINESS_
# REPORT.md) - with zero closed trades ever, this is a permanent cold-start deadlock
# (ARGUS_PREDICTION_EDGE_AND_LEARNING_IMPLEMENTATION_AUDIT.md). When true, a strategy refused only
# for that reason falls back to a regime-only bootstrap idea (no EV/stop/target) instead of no idea
# at all - still goes through the full ChiefTrader -> RiskEngine (24 gates) -> OMS pipeline
# unchanged. Do not enable to "see if it works" - only turn on when you specifically intend to seed
# a strategy's live track record under supervision.
QUANT_COLD_START_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED=false
# Scaffold only - no TradingAgents integration exists in this repository at all, and nothing reads
# this flag yet (src/server/research/tradingAgentsShadow.ts's only real implementation is a null
# adapter that always returns no opinion). Reserved for a future, separately-authorized adapter.
TRADING_AGENTS_SHADOW_ENABLED=false
# Gates QuantCoreBridge.ts's subscription to the local Java advisory Quant Core process
# (docs/architecture/JAVA_QUANT_CORE_MIGRATION_BLUEPRINT.md). Even when on, only forwards ticks
# and logs shadow-parity divergence - never calls emitTradeIdea. Advisory-only, no broker access.
QUANT_JAVA_CORE_ENABLED=false
# Session-Aware Trading Architecture Phase 5 (2026-09-05). Off by default. Gates RiskEngine gate 12's
# extended-hours OR-branch, the new gate 25 (extended_hours_execution_policy), and OMS's LIMIT-order
# construction for PRE_MARKET/AFTER_HOURS orders. See CLAUDE.md's 25-Gate RiskEngine Reference.
EXTENDED_HOURS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=false

# 2026-09-05, requires explicit, informed operator authorization - do not enable to "see if it
# works". TradePlanBuilder.emitTradePlanIdea() emits one TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED per PRIMARY-tier
# premarket TradePlan (one independent vote into the unchanged ChiefTrader consensus - same 0.75
# bar, min-2-independent-agents floor). This reverses this codebase's own default recommendation
# to wait for graded shadow-tracking evidence first (TradePlanShadowTracker) - see
# docs/audits/ARGUS_PREMARKET_TRADING_IMPLEMENTATION.md §11.6/§12 for the full reasoning before
# turning this on. Typically paired with EXTENDED_HOURS_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true above, since a
# premarket idea otherwise just waits for RTH to actually fill.
ARGUS_TRADE_PLAN_IDEAS_ENABLED=false
# 2026-09-09, requires explicit, informed operator authorization - do not enable to "see if it
# works". JavaQuantAdvisoryService.emitJavaQuantVoteIfEligible() emits one TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED
# per eligible Java factor-composite advisory (one independent vote into the unchanged ChiefTrader
# consensus - same 0.75 bar, min-2-independent-agents floor). This overrides this codebase's own
# documented Phase 3 precondition to wait for a real multi-week shadow-divergence-tracking window
# first - see docs/architecture/ARGUS_ARCHITECTURE.md's Java Quant Core section and
# JavaQuantAdvisoryService.ts's own header for the full reasoning before turning this on. Requires
# QUANT_JAVA_CORE_ENABLED=true to have any effect (the advisory analysis itself is gated on that
# flag, separately).
ARGUS_JAVA_QUANT_VOTE_ENABLED=false
# 2026-09-10, requires explicit, informed operator authorization - do not enable to "see if it
# works". JavaCoreEnsembleVoteService.emitJavaCoreEnsembleVoteIfEligible() emits one
# TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED per eligible Java CORE-strategy ensemble decision (CoreStrategyRunner's
# real, canonical-bar-owning RangeReversion/PullbackContinuation/MeanReversion/TrendFollowing/
# MomentumBreakout, correlation-adjusted via QuantEnsembleEngine.java) - one independent vote into
# the unchanged ChiefTrader consensus (same 0.75 bar, min-2-independent-agents floor). A distinct
# signal source from ARGUS_JAVA_QUANT_VOTE_ENABLED above (different Java engine, different
# features - not a duplicate vote). Real evidence base at the time this was enabled: ~99 shadow
# observations over ~4 hours (docs/audits/ARGUS_JAVA_QUANT_PHASE2_PRELIMINARY_PARITY_2026-09-10.md)
# - short of this deployment's own documented multi-week shadow-divergence-tracking precondition.
# See JavaCoreEnsembleVoteService.ts's own header for the full reasoning before turning this on.
# Requires QUANT_JAVA_CORE_ENABLED=true to have any effect.
ARGUS_JAVA_CORE_ENSEMBLE_VOTE_ENABLED=false
# 2026-10-05, requires explicit operator authorization - do not enable to "see if it works".
# InstitutionalStrategyVoteService emits one TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED per eligible evaluation of each
# institutional signal strategy below, as an independent vote into the UNCHANGED ChiefTrader
# consensus (same 0.75 bar, min-2-independent-agents floor) -> RiskEngine -> OMS -> BrokerManager
# spine. This is paper-verification wiring: it lets paper trading collect evidence on whether the
# strategies work. Successful paper execution is NOT evidence of profitability (house rule).
# Each flag needs its strategy's own Mission Control agent toggle (config/pipelineAgents.json) and
# QUANT_JAVA_CORE_ENABLED=true. INSTITUTIONAL_STAT_ARB is deliberately excluded - pairs need a
# pair universe and short-selling (see its header).
ARGUS_VOL_SCALED_MTF_MOMENTUM_VOTE_ENABLED=false
ARGUS_TS_MOMENTUM_12M_VOTE_ENABLED=false
ARGUS_MULTI_FACTOR_MOMENTUM_VOTE_ENABLED=false
# 2026-09-09, requires explicit, informed operator authorization - this is the single most
# significant override in this file. Overrides this codebase's own recommendation (see
# docs/audits/ARGUS_QUANTENGINE_EXPANSION_DESIGN_2026-09-09.md §16) to keep the standard
# 2-independent-agent floor until real correlation/outcome data exists to validate
# QuantEnsembleEngine.java's effectiveIndependentCount() math (its correlation matrix is a
# reviewed assumption, not measured). When true, a QuantEngine idea whose OWN internal ensemble
# (multiple strategy families, correlation-adjusted) clears a bar STRICTLY HIGHER than the normal
# 2-agent minimum (minQuantIndependentFamilies/minQuantIndependentEffectiveCount, tradingSafety.json)
# can satisfy ChiefTraderAgent.ts's independent-voice requirement without a second, separate agent.
# Every other gate (STRONG confidence threshold, hard vetoes, RiskEngine, OMS) is unchanged.
ARGUS_QUANT_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION_ENABLED=false
# Strategy-selection confluence guard (2026-09-11). Off by default. bestStrategyIdea() in
# StrategyEngine.ts picks the single highest-setupScore strategy and discards every other
# evaluation's side. When true, QuantSignalAgent.ts additionally checks whether the broader
# correlation-adjusted internal ensemble (same QuantEnsembleEngine.java math as
# ARGUS_QUANT_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION_ENABLED above) resolved to the OPPOSITE side and clears the
# SAME minQuantIndependentFamilies/minQuantIndependentEffectiveCount bar - if so, this cycle's idea
# is SUPPRESSED (not emitted), never flipped to the other side and never emitted with a lowered bar.
# Strictly more conservative than default behavior - can only ever prevent an emission, never add one.
ARGUS_STRATEGY_SELECTION_CONFLUENCE_GUARD_ENABLED=false
# Experimental SMC liquidity-sweep strategy in live Quant evaluateAll. Off by default.
# Backtests can still run the strategy via findStrategy without this flag.
QUANT_SMC_STRATEGY_ENABLED=false
# Other experimental Quant modules (also off). Each flag includes ONLY that module in live
# evaluateAll(); QUANT_SMC_STRATEGY_ENABLED does not enable these. findStrategy() backtests
# without the flag. Do not turn on to "see if it works".
QUANT_VWAP_STRUCTURE_ENABLED=false
QUANT_ORB_STRATEGY_ENABLED=false
QUANT_VWAP_REVERSION_ENABLED=false
QUANT_DONCHIAN_STRATEGY_ENABLED=false
QUANT_MA_CROSSOVER_ENABLED=false
QUANT_OSCILLATOR_MOMENTUM_ENABLED=false
QUANT_BOLLINGER_VOLATILITY_ENABLED=false
QUANT_PREVIOUS_PERIOD_BREAKOUT_ENABLED=false
QUANT_CANDLESTICK_REVERSAL_ENABLED=false
QUANT_GAP_STRATEGY_ENABLED=false
QUANT_FIBONACCI_PULLBACK_ENABLED=false
QUANT_VOLUME_CONFIRMATION_ENABLED=false
QUANT_SR_BOUNCE_ENABLED=false
QUANT_RELATIVE_STRENGTH_ENABLED=false
QUANT_STATISTICAL_REVERSION_ENABLED=false

# Optional multi-asset / penny overlay (src/server/multiAsset/). Default OFF = existing Argus
# behavior unchanged. Does not enable QUANT_ENGINE_ENABLED, LIVE, or OMS LIMIT orders.
# Penny/micro BUY ideas BLOCK while OMS remains MARKET-only (fail-closed, uncalibrated policy).
ARGUS_MULTI_ASSET_ENABLED=false
ARGUS_PENNY_STOCK_ENABLED=false

# Continuous opportunity + portfolio-intel loops. Default OFF.
# Opportunity loop expands IEX subscriptions from a bounded seed list (not a 5000-name tape).
# It never emits TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED. Portfolio intel requests ticks for open holdings and
# records HOLD/EXIT_CANDIDATE; executable SELL still uses PortfolioManager → RiskEngine → OMS.
# Does not lower ChiefTrader 0.75 / min-2-agents. Does not arm LIVE.
ARGUS_OPPORTUNITY_LOOP_ENABLED=false
# Crypto Expansion Phase 4 (2026-09-21). Real BTC-USD/ETH-USD REST quote polling into
# MarketDataWorker's existing observed-quote cache (config/runtimeIntervals.json
# cryptoMarketDataIngestionMs). PAPER/RESEARCH data only - no crypto broker exists to execute
# against yet (RiskEngine gate 12 still fails PAPER_BROKER_UNAVAILABLE for every crypto proposal).
# Requires ALPACA_API_KEY/ALPACA_SECRET_KEY (same credential crypto quotes already use, no separate
# key). Default OFF.
ARGUS_CRYPTO_MARKET_DATA_INGESTION_ENABLED=false
# Optional cheap rank ideas from OpportunityScreener (one vote into ChiefTrader, not consensus).
# Default OFF. Set true for Adaptive launch / momentum rotation so streamed movers can emit
# TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED. Does not lower ChiefTrader 0.75 / min-2. Does not call LLMs. Does not place orders.
ARGUS_OPPORTUNITY_IDEAS_ENABLED=false
# Fast Opportunity Lane (2026-10-05): parallel event-driven opportunity path for PAPER/research.
# Default OFF. When true, news/RVOL/price-acceleration events inject FastOpportunityCandidate
# objects that can reach strategy evaluation in seconds/minutes without waiting for the
# broad-universe refresh. NEVER bypasses ChiefTrader/RiskEngine/OMS. Fails closed for LIVE.
# PAPER/research only — formal promotion required before any LIVE use.
FAST_OPPORTUNITY_LANE_ENABLED=false
# Fast Opportunity Lane hung-lease quarantine (2026-10-09): after this many consecutive
# caller-timeouts for one symbol, or once a lease's age passes the max age, the lease is
# QUARANTINED - its concurrency slot returns to the pool while the dedup entry is kept, so a
# permanently hung evaluation can never wedge Fast Lane capacity and can never be duplicated.
# These are resource governors in config/tradingSafety.json (fastLaneHungLeaseMaxConsecutiveTimeouts,
# fastLaneHungLeaseMaxAgeMs), not env vars - documented here because they bound this lane's liveness.
# PAPER/research only — formal promotion required before any LIVE use.
# Jev shadow news scoring (Phase 1, 2026-10-06): when true, each news article is also
# scored by the Jev decision model in parallel (fire-and-forget) and the Jev-vs-LLM agreement
# is recorded to the jev_shadow_scores ledger for calibration measurement. Scores NEVER
# influence any trading decision. Requires JEV_API_KEY. Default OFF.
ARGUS_JEV_SHADOW_SCORING_ENABLED=false
# Jev confidence-gated escalation (Phase 2, 2026-10-06): when true, Jev scores each article
# FIRST and the LLM runs only on low Jev confidence, high-stakes articles, or Jev failure.
# Thresholds in config/tradingSafety.json (conservative initials pending Phase 1 calibration).
# Requires JEV_API_KEY. Default OFF. Never influences trading decisions directly.
ARGUS_JEV_ESCALATION_ENABLED=false
ARGUS_PORTFOLIO_INTEL_ENABLED=false
# Broad-universe discovery (MarketUniverseScanner.ts): real Alpaca tradable-assets list, batched
# snapshot + ADV screen (liquidity/price/spread filtered), merged into the same scan pool/gate the
# curated seed/watch lists already use. Never emits TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED itself. Makes real Alpaca
# API calls on each refresh - real cost/rate-limit exposure - so this is off by default; check
# GET /api/v2/continuous-intelligence/status's broadUniverse block after enabling.
ARGUS_BROAD_UNIVERSE_ENABLED=false
# Market-movers discovery funnel (MarketUniverseScanner.ts, refreshMoversCache()). Fetches the real
# Alpaca /v1beta1/screener/stocks/movers top-gainers/losers (moversFetchTopNPerSide=50 per side),
# then re-screens them through the same price/dollar-volume/spread/ADV gates the broad universe
# uses - a raw mover (e.g. a penny warrant) is never fed to the pipeline unfiltered. The surviving
# movers merge into the OpportunityDiscovery scan universe (moversTopNPerScan=20 per scan). Never
# emits TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED itself. Requires ARGUS_OPPORTUNITY_LOOP_ENABLED=true to actually
# refresh: the MarketUniverseScannerWorker refresh intervals (moversCacheTtlMs=300s) only run inside
# OpportunityDiscoveryWorker.start(). Makes real Alpaca API calls on each refresh - real
# cost/rate-limit exposure, off by default. PAPER implications: only widens which symbols the paper
# pipeline can subscribe to and evaluate; does not lower ChiefTrader 0.75 / min-2-agents, does not
# arm LIVE. Check GET /api/v2/continuous-intelligence/status's movers block after enabling.
ARGUS_MARKET_MOVERS_ENABLED=false
# News-catalyst discovery funnel (MarketUniverseScanner.ts, refreshNewsCatalystCache()). Proactively
# pulls symbols with real, reviewed catalyst evidence out of the in-process NewsCatalystStore
# (tradingBias != NEUTRAL and HIGH/MODERATE catalystStrength) into the discovery scan pool - closing
# the confirmed live gap where a genuine catalyst (SEI) was invisible to discovery because no agent
# had independently looked it up first. Screened through the exact same liquidity/price/spread/ADV
# gates as broad universe and movers (newsCatalystDiscoveryTopNPerScan=20 per scan). Zero new
# provider cost - reads the store NewsEngine's own ingest already fills; it does not start news
# ingest by itself. Requires ARGUS_OPPORTUNITY_LOOP_ENABLED=true to actually refresh
# (newsCatalystDiscoveryCacheTtlMs=300s, same worker as above). Default OFF. Never emits
# TRADE_IDEA_GENERATED itself.
ARGUS_NEWS_CATALYST_DISCOVERY_ENABLED=false
# ExitIntelligenceEngine (ARGUS_EXIT_INTELLIGENCE_PLAN.md): an additional, lower-priority exit
# check PortfolioMonitor consults only after every existing check (quant stop/target, thesis
# invalidation, generic take-profit/trailing-stop) already found nothing this cycle. Never places
# orders itself; a TAKE_PROFIT/EXIT/EMERGENCY_EXIT opinion still goes through the normal
# PortfolioManager -> ChiefTrader risk-exit bypass -> RiskEngine -> OMS path. Unvalidated/
# unbacktested new decision model - default OFF.
ARGUS_EXIT_INTELLIGENCE_ENABLED=false
# AI Cost Governor / Project A (docs/audits/ARGUS_PROJECT_A_AI_COST_GOVERNOR_DESIGN_NOTE.md):
# reorders (never removes-to-empty on ambiguity) the already-routable provider list AIRouter was
# about to try, preferring cheaper cost tiers first per config/aiCostGovernor.json's reviewed
# per-agent policy. Two independent flags - master enable computes+logs shadow decisions only
# (AI_COST_GOVERNOR_SHADOW_COMPARISON observability events); real routing only changes once the
# second flag is ALSO true. Never touches ChiefTrader/RiskEngine/OMS/consensus/routeConsensus.
AI_COST_GOVERNOR_ENABLED=false
AI_COST_GOVERNOR_LIVE_ENABLED=false
# Optional Bull/Bear qualitative notes in ChiefTrader debate. Off by default.
# Does not invent prices/EV; does not bypass RiskEngine.
QUANT_BULL_BEAR_ENABLED=false

# Local Chronos/Kronos + FinBERT (scripts/local_ai_service.py). npm run dev starts this unless
# ARGUS_SKIP_CHRONOS=true. First boot downloads amazon/chronos-t5-mini if the HF cache is empty.
LOCAL_AI_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8008
LOCAL_AI_SERVICE_PORT=8008
ARGUS_SKIP_CHRONOS=false
# Ollama local LLMs. npm run dev runs `ollama serve` if port 11434 is free and ollama is on PATH.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
ARGUS_SKIP_OLLAMA=false
# Headless engine boot (argus-cli start / server.ts — not just npm run dev):
# when true, the engine itself probes Ollama (11434) and Chronos/Kronos (8008/health)
# at boot and spawns them if down (`ollama serve` / `python scripts/local_ai_service.py`).
# Probes first — never starts a duplicate. Opt-in per deployment; off by default.
ARGUS_START_LOCAL_MODELS=false
ARGUS_START_CHRONOS=false
# Skip spawning OpenAlice Guardian even if a checkout exists.
ARGUS_SKIP_OPENALICE=false
# Skip spawning / opening IBKR Gateway.
ARGUS_SKIP_IBKR=false
# 2026-10-05: SEC EDGAR Form 4 insider-transaction scraper. Polls the free SEC EDGAR
# JSON API (public domain, no vendor) for Form 4 filings on Argus's tracked symbols
# and stores them in insider_transactions. Data plumbing only - emits no trade ideas.
# Respects SEC rate limits (sequential requests, 500ms spacing, proper User-Agent).
ARGUS_SEC_EDGAR_FORM4_ENABLED=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CROSS-CUTTING DEFECT HUNT 2026-10-10 — env-var documentation sweep.
# Every process.env read in src/ and scripts/ now resolves to a documented entry
# in this file, or to a justified exclusion listed in section J below.
# Sections: A. Production-critical runtime & safety | B. Presentation adapters |
# C. AI & news providers | D. Broker credentials & market-data keys |
# E. Paths / pid-state files / observability | F. CLI, watchdog & engine launcher |
# G. Research / replay / python | H. Dev-ecosystem orchestrator & diagnostics |
# I. Test-only & fault-injection (never set in production) | J. Justified exclusions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- A. PRODUCTION-CRITICAL RUNTIME & SAFETY --------------------------------
# SQLite database path. Default: <resolved db dir>/argus.db (see resolveDbDir).
# Integration tests and the synthetic-session engine set this to an isolated file;
# production/dev behavior is unchanged when unset. NEVER point a test at data/argus.db.
# ARGUS_DB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/argus.db
# Isolation marker. 'true' = this process is a synthetic simulation, never production.
# Triggers productionRuntimePathGuard + syntheticSimulationDbGuard: the process FAILS LOUD
# if it would touch real runtime-identity files or the production DB. Set ONLY by the
# synthetic-session engine itself (SyntheticSessionEngine sets it at spawn). Never set
# this in production, dev, or paper operation.
# SYNTHETIC_SIMULATION=true
# 5-layer live arming, layer 5 (per-process LIVE arm). SyntheticSimulationSafety FAILS a
# synthetic session outright if this is 'true'. PAPER ONLY: never set LIVE_ARM=true.
# LIVE_ARM=false
# Tags paper-trading validation runs (PaperTradingValidation). Default ARGUS_PAPER_EXPERIMENT_001.
# ARGUS_PAPER_EXPERIMENT_ID=ARGUS_PAPER_EXPERIMENT_001
# Paper-broker order-registry memory bound. On by default; set 'false' ONLY for forensic
# debugging (registries return to unbounded growth).
# ARGUS_PAPER_BROKER_ORDER_EVICTION=false
# Max entries in the paper-broker order registry before terminal orders are evicted.
# Positive integer; default 5000. See brokerMemory.ts resolvePaperBrokerOrderRegistryMax().
# ARGUS_PAPER_BROKER_ORDER_REGISTRY_MAX=5000
# Cap for the OMS warn-once registry. Positive integer; default 1000.
# ARGUS_OMS_WARN_ONCE_MAX=1000
# News pipeline master switch. Default ON; set 'false' to keep NewsEngine from starting
# (ArgusCoreBoot, SystemBootstrap). Synthetic sessions force it off.
# ARGUS_NEWS_ENGINE_ENABLED=false
# Post-market analysis job. Default ON; 'false' disables (SystemBootstrap).
# ARGUS_POST_MARKET_ANALYSIS_ENABLED=false
# 'true' disables market-data WebSocket ownership (marketDataWsOwnership). Synthetic
# sessions force it on-true; use in production only to run fully WS-free.
# ARGUS_DISABLE_MARKET_DATA_WS=true
# 'true' disables heap-snapshot capture (observability/heapSnapshotCapture). Synthetic
# sessions force it on-true.
# ARGUS_DISABLE_HEAP_SNAPSHOTS=true
# Master switch for the AI call governor. Env override wins over
# config/aiCallGovernor.json's aiGovernorEnabled (config/aiCallGovernor.ts envOverride).
# ARGUS_AI_CALL_GOVERNOR_ENABLED=false
# Env override for config/aiCallGovernor.json's jevEnabled (Jev advisory path).
# ARGUS_JEV_ENABLED=false
# 'true' enables the MODERATE consensus tier (ChiefTraderAgent/ModerateTierEvaluator).
# Strictly MORE conservative than the STRONG path (same 0.75 bar, min-2-independent,
# plus calibration-trust gates). Never lowers thresholds. Default off.
# CONSENSUS_MODERATE_TIER_ENABLED=true
# 'true' enables the research paper-testing parameter overlay (paperTestingOverlay).
# Data plumbing only - emits no trade ideas, places no orders. Default off.
# QUANT_PAPER_TESTING_PARAMS=true
# Comma-separated asset classes treated as valid trade-idea symbols. Default EQUITY.
# Crypto Expansion mandate (2026-09-22); read live on every validateInstrument.
# ARGUS_TRADEABLE_ASSET_CLASSES=EQUITY,CRYPTO
# Build SHA stamped into decision_provenance rows (decisionProvenance.ts). Set by CI /
# release tooling; informational only, never gates behavior.
# ARGUS_BUILD_SHA=

# --- B. PRESENTATION / RUNTIME ADAPTERS --------------------------------------
# HTTP REST adapter. Default ON; Engine CLI requires it. 'false' disables the API.
# API_ENABLED=false
# Vite/static SPA. Default ON unless headless/engine. 'false' skips the Web UI;
# trading core + REST API still run.
# WEB_UI_ENABLED=false
# WebSocket EventBus fan-out adapter. Optional; default ON. Not required for trading.
# Requires API_ENABLED. 'false' disables WS fan-out.
# WS_ENABLED=false
# Dedicated engine-daemon process (scripts/argus-engine.ts). 'true' implies headless
# presentation; the SAME Argus Core boots either way - never a separate trading engine.
# ARGUS_ENGINE=true

# --- C. AI & NEWS PROVIDERS ---------------------------------------------------
# Fallback for JEV_API_KEY (JevDecisionProvider, NewsEngine). Prefer JEV_API_KEY;
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY is the legacy alias. Key comes from the process env only - never
# committed, never read from .env files by the app.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Override the Jev/TypeSafe API base URL (JevProvider, JevDecisionProvider).
# JEV_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.example
# Moonshot (Kimi) provider key. AIRouter resolves the "Kimi" model family to this.
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# Passed through to the autohedge worker's environment by scripts/ecosystem-dev.ts.
# JUPITER_API_KEY=
# Ollama port for scripts/lib/ollamaLauncher.ts. Default 11434.
# OLLAMA_PORT=11434

# --- D. BROKER CREDENTIALS & MARKET-DATA KEYS ---------------------------------
# Boot-time Alpaca secret import (persistEncryptedSecrets): upserted into the encrypted
# broker store alongside ALPACA_API_KEY and mirrored to ALPACA_SECRET_KEY for the
# session. Prefer the Setup Wizard / Settings UI; env is the unattended path.
# ALPACA_API_SECRET=
# SnapshotScanner fallbacks: APCA_API_KEY_ID is tried after ALPACA_API_KEY, and
# APCA_API_SECRET_KEY after ALPACA_API_KEY's secret counterpart. Legacy Alpaca naming.
# APCA_API_KEY_ID=
# APCA_API_SECRET_KEY=

# --- E. PATHS / PID-STATE FILES / OBSERVABILITY --------------------------------
# Override for the crash-log file (crashLog.ts). Default under the runtime dir.
# ARGUS_CRASH_LOG_PATH=/var/log/argus/crash.log
# Override for the engine pid file (enginePid.ts).
# ARGUS_ENGINE_PID_PATH=/run/argus/engine.pid
# Override for the watchdog pid file (watchdogPid.ts).
# ARGUS_WATCHDOG_PID_PATH=/run/argus/watchdog.pid
# Override for the watchdog state file (scripts/lib/watchdogStateStore.ts).
# ARGUS_WATCHDOG_STATE_PATH=/run/argus/watchdog-state.json
# Watchdog heartbeat path read by StartupHealthRegistry.
# ARGUS_WATCHDOG_HEARTBEAT_PATH=/run/argus/watchdog.heartbeat
# Override for the maintenance-state file (maintenanceState.ts; also read by the watchdog).
# ARGUS_MAINTENANCE_STATE_PATH=/run/argus/maintenance-state.json
# Repo root override. Default: process.cwd() (repoPaths.ts).
# ARGUS_REPO_ROOT=/opt/argus-trading
# Replay store directory (replayStore.ts). Default under the runtime data dir.
# ARGUS_REPLAY_DIR=/data/argus/replays
# Research warehouse (parquet) directory (parquetStore.ts). Default under the runtime data dir.
# ARGUS_RESEARCH_DIR=/data/argus/research
# Override for the Fincept terminal cache DB path (FinceptCacheAdapter).
# FINCEPT_CACHE_DB_PATH=/data/argus/fincept-cache.db

# --- F. CLI, WATCHDOG & ENGINE LAUNCHER ----------------------------------------
# argus-cli base URL (scripts/argus-cli.ts). Default http://127.0.0.1:3000.
# ARGUS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Watchdog base URL (scripts/argusWatchdog.ts). Falls back to BASE_URL, then 127.0.0.1:3000.
# ARGUS_CLI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Legacy fallback for the watchdog base URL when ARGUS_CLI_BASE_URL is unset.
# BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# argus-cli session file path. Default under the repo root (argus-cli.ts).
# ARGUS_CLI_SESSION_FILE=/home/argus/.argus-cli-session.json
# argus-cli HTTP fetch timeout, ms. Default 20000 (10000 on the health path).
# ARGUS_CLI_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
# argus-cli `start` wait-for-ready timeout, ms. Default 150000.
# ARGUS_CLI_START_TIMEOUT_MS=150000
# Dev token for mutating /api/v1|/api/v2 calls when AUTH_PASSWORD is unset
# (X-Argus-Dev-Token header). Min 8 chars; honored if pre-set, otherwise a random
# per-process token is generated (AuthConfig.ensureDevToken). Never use a real
# password here.
# ARGUS_DEV_TOKEN=
# 'true' opts scripts/argus-engine.ts into the langgraph-research supervisor path.
# LANGGRAPH_RESEARCH_ENABLED=true

# --- G. RESEARCH / REPLAY / PYTHON ----------------------------------------------
# 'true' enables research-parquet writes (experimentLedger, HistoricalDataProviderRegistry,
# ingestAlpacaWarehouse, parquetStore). Default off - research stays read-only.
# ARGUS_WRITE_RESEARCH_PARQUET=true
# Python interpreter for VectorBTService. Default 'python'.
# ARGUS_PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3
# 'true' allows vectorbt-backed paths to run under vitest (VectorBTService,
# ingestAlpacaWarehouse refuse under VITEST otherwise). Test/dev only.
# ARGUS_TEST_ALLOW_VECTORBT=true
# VibeTrading research MCP adapter URL (VibeTradingResearchAdapter). Default
# http://127.0.0.1:8900. Read-only research/verification - never execution.
# VIBE_TRADING_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8900
# OpenAlice web UI URL (OpenAliceWorkspace). Default http://127.0.0.1:47331.
# OPENALICE_WEB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:47331
# INTERNAL - set by the dev launcher (devWithOpenAlice) when the OpenAlice spawn fails;
# read by ModelRuntimeManager / argus-ecosystem-status. Do not set manually.
# OPENALICE_LAUNCH_ERROR=
# Dev launcher: 'false' skips the IBKR probe step (devWithOpenAlice). Default probes.
# ARGUS_PROBE_IBKR=false

# --- H. DEV-ECOSYSTEM ORCHESTRATOR (npm run dev) & DIAGNOSTICS -------------------
# `npm run dev` -> scripts/ecosystem-dev.ts only. Missing tools warn and continue;
# none of these touch the trading path.
# AUTOHEDGE_CMD=/opt/autohedge/bin/autohedge
# AUTOHEDGE_WORKSPACE_DIR=/opt/autohedge/agent_workspace
# FINCEPT_CMD=/opt/fincept/bin/fincept-terminal
# IBKR market-data diagnostic probe (scripts/ibkr_market_data_diagnostic.ts).
# IBKR_DIAGNOSTIC_CLIENT_ID=999
# IBKR_DIAGNOSTIC_WINDOW_MS=15000
# Optional: 1=live 2=frozen 3=delayed 4=delayed-frozen.
# IBKR_DIAGNOSTIC_MARKET_DATA_TYPE=3
# Dev launcher: 'true' opens the IBKR Client Portal login page in a browser on startup.
# IBKR_OPEN_BROWSER=true

# --- I. TEST-ONLY & FAULT-INJECTION (never set in production) --------------------
# Arms the fault-injection framework: ONLY the exact value '1' satisfies
# FaultInjectionGate.assertFaultInjectionEnabled(). No production entry point sets it;
# the npm test scripts set it explicitly. A static test FAILS if any production file
# outside fault-injection/** reads it. Never export this in a shell profile.
# ARGUS_FAULT_INJECTION=1
# Pins the fast-check seed for property tests (propertyInvariants.test.ts,
# positionFillEvidence.property.test.ts) so CI/local runs can reproduce a failure.
# ARGUS_FC_SEED=12345
# Test flag consumed by JevClassificationTask.test.ts (flagEnvVar) to exercise the
# Jev classification task path in isolation.
# ARGUS_JEV_TEST_TASK_ENABLED=true
# Test-only shell-path override used by shellCli.protection.test.ts.
# ARGUS_BASH=/bin/bash
# Legacy/test-only credential name; only referenced by SecretRedaction.test.ts to
# prove redaction. Not read by any production code path.
# APP_PASSWORD=
# NOT A REAL VARIABLE - negative control in AIRouter.test.ts proving "Claude"
# resolves to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Never set this expecting it to work.
# CLAUDE_API_KEY=

# --- J. JUSTIFIED EXCLUSIONS (read in code, NOT Argus config - do not add) --------
# ALPACA_            - not a real read; appears only inside a BrokerManager.ts comment
#                      ("process.env.ALPACA_*") describing the AlpacaBroker fallback family.
# HOME / PATH / USERPROFILE - OS-provided process environment, not Argus configuration.
# VITEST             - set automatically by the Vitest runner itself on every test run;
#                      used by productionRuntimePathGuard as the isolation signal.
# NO_COLOR           - standard CLI convention honored by colorized output; not Argus config.
# JAVA_HOME          - standard JVM toolchain variable used to locate java for
#                      quant-core-java builds; not Argus configuration.

# --- Wall-clock soak verdict bounds (scripts/soak/threeHourSoakChild.ts only; never read by the engine) ---
# The soak verdict is resource-gated: it fails if any bound below is exceeded, and zero iteration
# errors alone is NOT a pass. Values shown are the code defaults; uncomment to tune.
# SOAK_MAX_RSS_MB=2048
# SOAK_MAX_RSS_DELTA_MB=512
# SOAK_MAX_EVENT_LOOP_P95_MS=100
# SOAK_MAX_DB_GROWTH_BYTES=1073741824
# SOAK_MAX_WAL_BYTES=104857600
